Drive unified manual progress through the sockets manual progress engine.
Discovery retains FI_PROGRESS_CONTROL_UNIFIED, but the internal engine only
distinguishes automatic and manual progress. Leaving the unified value in
that field disables both CQ-driven progress and the automatic worker.

Based on ofiwg/libfabric v2.7.0.

--- a/prov/sockets/src/sock_dom.c
+++ b/prov/sockets/src/sock_dom.c
@@ -174,6 +174,8 @@
 
 	if (info->domain_attr->data_progress == FI_PROGRESS_UNSPEC)
 		sock_domain->progress_mode = FI_PROGRESS_AUTO;
+	else if (info->domain_attr->data_progress == FI_PROGRESS_CONTROL_UNIFIED)
+		sock_domain->progress_mode = FI_PROGRESS_MANUAL;
 	else
 		sock_domain->progress_mode = info->domain_attr->data_progress;
 
